nora (docs): Quick ask — adding a short "Errors & Mitigations" note for 429s/timeouts/context limits. Need tiny py/js snippets and a customer checklist.

felix (eng-runtime): Keep guidance: honor Retry-After if present; else exponential backoff with full jitter; after ~3 attempts fail to lighter model. Note KV cache cold starts can cause spikes, recommend a warmup pass.

sam (devex): JS AbortController snippet: ```js
async function callWithRetry(url, opts = {}) {
  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
    const ctrl = new AbortController();
    const timer = setTimeout(() => ctrl.abort(), opts.timeout || 60000);
    try {
      const res = await fetch(url, { ...opts, signal: ctrl.signal });
      clearTimeout(timer);
      if (res.status === 429) {
        const ra = res.headers.get('Retry-After');
        const wait = ra ? Number(ra) : Math.min(Math.pow(2, i) + Math.random(), 30);
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, wait * 1000));
        continue;
      }
      if (!res.ok) throw new Error('http');
      return await res.json();
    } catch (e) {
      clearTimeout(timer);
      if (e.name === 'AbortError') await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, (Math.pow(2, i) + Math.random()) * 1000));
      else throw e;
    }
  }
}
```

